WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.917
Work is the oldest technology we have. The tools keep changing.

2
00:00:04.917 --> 00:00:09.624
The five questions behind them never have. How do we organise?

3
00:00:09.624 --> 00:00:16.243
What is the work worth? Who is ready? How do people grow? And where do we find them?

4
00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:31.944
Göbekli Tepe, Anatolia. Around 9500 BCE. Before the farm, there was the team.

5
00:00:31.944 --> 00:00:37.503
Hunter-gatherers raised rings of stone pillars weighing several tonnes.

6
00:00:37.503 --> 00:00:39.008
Nobody lifts one alone.

7
00:00:39.008 --> 00:00:44.066
So somebody had to decide who cuts, who hauls, and who feeds the crew.

8
00:00:44.066 --> 00:00:46.781
Question one: how do we organise?

9
00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:57.368
Uruk, Mesopotamia. Around 3300 BCE.

10
00:00:57.368 --> 00:01:04.125
Among the oldest writing we have is a clay record of rations owed to workers.

11
00:01:04.125 --> 00:01:09.050
The first payslip was paid in beer. Pay was written down before poetry was.

12
00:01:09.050 --> 00:01:15.981
And when the rations arrived late at Deir el-Medina, the tomb builders put down their tools.

13
00:01:15.981 --> 00:01:21.196
The first recorded strike. Question two: what is the work worth?

14
00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:28.276
Imperial China. Merit, not birth.

15
00:01:28.276 --> 00:01:36.849
Public office goes to whoever passes a written examination: long rows of single cells, one candidate in each.

16
00:01:36.849 --> 00:01:41.500
The system runs for about thirteen hundred years, until 1905.

17
00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:43.986
Question three: who is ready?

18
00:01:55.800 --> 00:02:00.167
Medieval Europe, and the craft guilds. Nobody is born ready.

19
00:02:00.167 --> 00:02:02.858
The apprentice spends years beside a master.

20
00:02:02.858 --> 00:02:05.309
The journeyman takes the craft on the road.

21
00:02:05.309 --> 00:02:11.347
The master is judged by peers on one piece of work: the original meaning of a masterpiece.

22
00:02:11.347 --> 00:02:14.038
Question four: how do people grow?

23
00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:28.909
Philadelphia. A job becomes a coordinate.

24
00:02:28.909 --> 00:02:32.895
In 1911, Frederick Taylor put a stopwatch on the task.

25
00:02:32.895 --> 00:02:39.165
In 1943, Edward Hay founded a firm on a harder idea: weigh the job, not the person.

26
00:02:39.165 --> 00:02:49.104
By the early 1950s, its Guide Charts scored any role on three factors: know-how, problem solving and accountability.

27
00:02:49.104 --> 00:02:52.619
Points become a grade, and a grade becomes a pay range.

28
00:02:52.619 --> 00:02:58.066
Job evaluation is still the backbone of grading and pay benchmarking.

29
00:03:05.800 --> 00:03:10.400
The knowledge economy. When the asset is a mind, you go and find it.

30
00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:15.441
In 1959, Peter Drucker describes a workforce paid to think.

31
00:03:15.441 --> 00:03:21.141
In 1969, Lester Korn and Richard Ferry open an office in Los Angeles.

32
00:03:21.141 --> 00:03:24.033
The door already says International.

33
00:03:24.033 --> 00:03:30.286
In 1973, Harvard's David McClelland argues for testing what predicts success in the job.

34
00:03:30.286 --> 00:03:33.102
Question five: where do we find them?

35
00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:46.446
Five answers. One firm. For most of history, each question had its own specialists.

36
00:03:46.446 --> 00:03:51.836
Then the threads met. Lominger brought leadership competencies.

37
00:03:51.836 --> 00:03:55.599
PDI Ninth House brought assessment and coaching.

38
00:03:55.599 --> 00:03:59.632
Hay Group, in 2015, brought rewards and organisation.

39
00:03:59.632 --> 00:04:04.520
And in 2026, AMS brought talent acquisition and outsourced recruitment at scale.

40
00:04:04.520 --> 00:04:07.632
All five threads, moving at once.

41
00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:30.224
2026. The tools changed again. The questions did not.

42
00:04:30.224 --> 00:04:35.408
AI is rewriting how work gets done, faster than any shift before it.

43
00:04:35.408 --> 00:04:38.914
The answers still start in the same five places.

44
00:04:38.914 --> 00:04:47.460
Korn Ferry Talent Suite, launched in January 2026, brings five decades of the firm's data and method onto one platform.
